  "tagline": "MultiValue database that compiles Pick BASIC to native code, now part of Rocket's MV portfolio.",
  "description": "jBASE is a MultiValue (Pick-compatible) database and application environment whose distinguishing idea is compiling Pick BASIC to C/C++ and then native executables, and running on ordinary Linux, Unix and Windows rather than a Pick virtual machine. Its jEDI layer can also store MultiValue files in other back ends. It was long the platform under Temenos's T24 core-banking software and many smaller vertical packages. Zumasys bought it in 2015 and Rocket Software acquired the Zumasys portfolio in 2021; 6.2.1 (October 2024) added a D3 migration path and 6.2.2 brought Windows Server 2025 support, journaling v2 and Reality conversion tooling. It is maintained, but almost entirely for existing applications.",
